<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .header-logo {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .logo-icon {
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    margin-right: 15px;
  }
  .logo-text h1 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .media-contact {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .media-contact strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <div class="logo-icon">
      <!-- Placeholder for logo icon -->
    </div>
    <div class="logo-text">
      <h1><span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span></h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 10px;">FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE</h2>

  <div class="media-contact">
    <strong>Media Contact:</strong>
    <span data-field="media_contact.name">{{ media_contact.name }}</span>
    <span data-field="media_contact.title">{{ media_contact.title }}</span>
    <span data-field="media_contact.phone">{{ media_contact.phone }}</span> | <span data-field="media_contact.email">{{ media_contact.email }}</span>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <span data-field="location">{{ location }}</span>, MA — <span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span> honored more than <span data-field="number_of_rabbi">{{ number_of_rabbi }}</span> rabbis, cantors, and Jewish educators during <span data-field="event_name">{{ event_name }}</span> in June, which included the ordination of <span data-field="number_of_rabbi">{{ number_of_rabbi }}</span> rabbis and three cantors. The graduates, who completed their final year-and-a-half of coursework online, will go on to work in Reform and Conservative synagogues, hills, schools, and pastoral care settings across the United States.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    "We have learned this year in such deep ways—ways we never would have imagined—that even when we are not physically together, we do not stand alone." We do not journey alone," said <span data-field="speaker_name">{{ speaker_name }}</span>. "Today, we celebrate the hope for renewal that becomes possible when we watch carefully for the lights that are kindled by those around us and add to that light by kindling our own fires."
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    Degrees conferred included Master of Arts in Jewish Studies, Master of Jewish Education, Master of Jewish Liberal Studies program, and Master of Jewish Education-Parades Educators Program. Students presented their <span data-field="thesis_type">{{ thesis_type }}</span> on June 3. Commencement was live-streamed on <span data-field="streaming_platform">{{ streaming_platform }}</span>. Ordination ceremonies followed at <span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span> and were also streamed on the College's YouTube channel.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span> also bestowed honorary degrees on <span data-field="honoree_name_1">{{ honoree_name_1 }}</span>, a pioneer in the field of Jewish healing and contemporary spirituality, and <span data-field="honoree_name_2">{{ honoree_name_2 }}</span>, a senior research fellow at the Shalom Hartman Institute, both of whom offered messages to the graduates.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    Placements include <span data-field="placement_1">{{ placement_1 }}</span> at <span data-field="placement_1_location">{{ placement_1_location }}</span>, <span data-field="placement_2">{{ placement_2 }}</span> as associate rabbi at <span data-field="placement_2_location">{{ placement_2_location }}</span> in Livingston, N.J.; <span data-field="placement_3">{{ placement_3 }}</span> as director of Jewish Education at the University of Minnesota Hill and Herzi Camp in Minneapolis, Minn., <span data-field="placement_4">{{ placement_4 }}</span> as a faculty member and Beit midrash instructor at <span data-field="placement_4_institution">{{ placement_4_institution }}</span>; amongst others. Cantor Ken Richmond of Temple Israel in Natick, Mass. is now a rav-hazzan.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span> is an innovative national institute for Jewish learning and leadership based in <span data-field="location_state">{{ location_state }}</span>, Massachusetts. We are dedicated to Jewish literacy, creativity, and community, and a world of dignity and compassion for all. Our students are future rabbis, cantors, and educators, and people at every stage of life who love to learn. Together, we are infusing Jewish life with substance, spirit, beauty, imagination, and a sense of purpose. Learn more at <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span>.
  </p>
</div>